# the text form of an ELF model
#
# the file as the model holds it, in file order: the file header, the program
# headers, the section headers with each compression header, then the
# contents of the sections that hold records. every record and field takes the
# name llvm-readobj gives it, so the output lines up field by field with what
# llvm-readobj prints for the same file. the names and nesting are those of
# LLVM 23, the release the ELF tables are generated from. a value with a name
# prints its name and its number, from the generic tables and from the tables
# of the machine the file is for. a flags field prints the names of its bits,
# and e_flags names its bits by the trait rows of the file's architecture.
# the dump prints what the model holds and decodes nothing the reader did not,
# so a value the model keeps raw prints raw.

